  "question": {
    "text": "In the given figure magnetic field at the center of ring&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. Now it is turned through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>xx</mi><mo>'</mo></math> axis, so that two semicircular parts are mutually perpendicular. The new value of magnetic field (in Tesla) at centre is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></math>. Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/630123-2.JPG\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 200px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>In 2<sup>nd</sup>&nbsp;case,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>",
